{"kind":"report","text":"MCP host requirements audit for 20fcc6e7, under promise 0c59b6fb.\n\nThe audit checks dap at main 04f4af48 against published requirements,\nfrom documentation and source only. No account, registration,\ndeployment or live check ran. Files, in\n~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-02-mcp-host-requirements-audit:\n\n- matrix.md, SHA256 568e3c4b86c327e51b10ba45401986cc1337cd86c33455cb4d7d3d435e3995c0\n- corrections.md, SHA256 de6f178050b6653b3be65992bf4f9eef42bf1ad522dc34a96c2b5b50bc3f0dda\n\ncorrections.md fixes one wrong finding. matrix.md says no dap card has\nrendered in Claude Desktop, but Hugh read the diff and interdiff cards\nthere on 1 November (e278f412, ae716086).\n\nVerdict by host:\n\n- ChatGPT cannot connect. Hosted MCP is closed, and ChatGPT needs\n  OAuth, which dap has not built.\n- Claude web cannot connect, for the same two reasons. Claude Desktop\n  connects, calls tools and renders cards over local stdio.\n- Goose Desktop 1.57.0 connects and calls tools over stdio. Its cards\n  fail at packages/mcp/browser/bridge.ts:84. Goose's bridge, from\n  @mcp-ui/client 6.1.0, bundles ext-apps 0.3.1, and the audit reads\n  from that source that it replies 2025-11-21. No live run has\n  captured that value yet.\n- Gemini consumer cannot connect. It needs the hosted endpoint, OAuth\n  with Google Account Linking, a tool list fixed at registration, JSON\n  in text content, and Google's preview access. Its MCP Apps UI is\n  beta, and Google may ignore UI resources. The matrix reports that\n  limitation apart from connection and authentication.\n\nRemediation, by the number of hosts each item unblocks:\n\n1. Accept the version the host returns in the card bridge, as the\n   official SDK does. Request d23fb0b6 already covers this. Read\n   matrix.md section 3 item 1 before you start it.\n2. Open hosted MCP on one named Worker. That is my decision, after\n   item 4.\n3. Serve cards from the hosted endpoint. packages/mcp/src/hosted.ts\n   builds the hosted service without any card source.\n4. Make /mcp an OAuth resource server: discovery metadata, a 401 that\n   points to it, and tokens bound to the /mcp URL.\n5. Build the authorization server. The member who signs the existing\n   create or bearer request gives consent. It needs client\n   registration (CIMD and DCR) and each host's redirect URIs.\n\nThe matrix rules out two shortcuts, because each widens who may act:\nGoogle's machine-to-machine client credentials, and Claude's\norganization-wide shared header credential.\n\nItems 3 to 5 wait for Hugh to read the matrix. I file them as builder\nrequests only after he does. The live validation stays deferred and\nunscheduled under 5066018a.\n\nBuilder: please ratify this report so 20fcc6e7 closes. Ratify this\nact's own ID. Nothing you do waits on it.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}